# AI Tools Boundaries

## Current layers

| Layer | Responsibility | Must not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ToolDefinition` | Schema / contract only | Execute handlers, call providers |
| `ToolRegistry` | Store `ToolBinding` only | Call handlers, validate args |
| `ToolValidator` | Validate `tool_name` + raw args | Call handlers, invoke tools |
| `ToolExecutor` | Validate → resolve binding → invoke once → JSON-safe result | Import Character/OpenAI/FastAPI; swallow unexpected exceptions |
| `AgentService` | Future orchestration between LLM and tools | Live in provider or registry layers |
| Provider | Vendor API only | Own tool registry/execution policy |

## Rules

- No lower generic tool layer imports a higher orchestration layer or concrete domain tool class.
- No OpenAI-specific fields in generic tool execution results.
- Unknown tools and invalid arguments must not invoke handlers.
- Unexpected programming errors must propagate (or be wrapped without losing cause) — never silently converted to success=False via bare `except Exception`.
